# Specifications are hashed. BOOTSTRAP-EXIT-CRITERIA.sha256 in this repository
# pins BOOTSTRAP-EXIT-CRITERIA.md by SHA-256, and under core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, the hash stops matching, and nothing
# says "line endings": it reads as the specification having been altered.
#
# `-text` rather than `text eol=lf`. Do not convert in either direction. The
# point is that these bytes never change.
specs/** -text

# Orchestration scripts are normalised to LF because they get hashed too. The
# review protocol freezes a script and its negative controls as a review
# target with a recorded SHA-256, and a checkout that rewrote them would make
# that hash stop verifying.
*.py text eol=lf
